gguf-rco step 6e: the CUDA IQ3_S path (dequantize_block_iq3_s, vec_dot_iq3_s_q8_1)
reads its magnitudes from iq3xs_grid, the format's pre-2024-03 table in quarter
units whose top value is 62 (= 15.5); the format since llama.cpp #5829 and the
gguf reference say 15. Every element with the top magnitude (4.24 % of the IQ3_S
weights, measured) was 31/30 too large on the dequantise and MMVQ paths. The top
magnitude becomes 60 (= 4 * 15): byte 0x3e -> 0x3c in every entry of the table;
the scale d * (2 s + 1) / 4 and the index contract are unchanged. Do NOT also
apply llama.cpp #5829's 1.033 factor to d: that factor belongs to the
quantiser and is already inside the file's scales; applying it here would put
a 3.3 % error on every weight instead of removing one from 4 % of them.
Applies after 0022, 0023 and 0024.

